+      "title": "DRAFT: volume factor in Ising thermal coupling",
+      "statement": "DRAFT, independent mathematical review pending. Fix 0<beta<beta_c and dimension d. For zero-field free-boundary box magnetization M_n, let v_n be its volume, chi_n=kappa_2(M_n)/v_n and B_n=-kappa_4(M_n)/kappa_2(M_n)^2. If chi_n->chi>0, kappa_4(M_n)/v_n->-A and 0<xi<infinity, then lim_n B_n v_n/xi^d=A/(chi^2 xi^d)=g_+(beta). In particular B_n->0 at fixed beta does not imply g_+(beta)=0.",
+      "proof_text": null,
+      "assumptions": [
+        "Thermodynamic limit at each fixed subcritical beta precedes the critical limit.",
+        "Stated second- and fourth-cumulant density limits exist and are finite.",
+        "Correlation length xi is the source's exponential length for the infinite-volume law."
+      ],
