+      "logical_name": "ising-variance-weighted-lee-yang-zero-mass-criterion",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "DRAFT: variance mass of Lee-Yang zeros at correlation-volume scale",
+      "statement": "DRAFT, independent mathematical review pending. For the same finite-volume Lee-Yang magnetization, list positive imaginary zeros alpha_j with multiplicity. Put r_j=alpha_j sqrt(chi_n xi^d) and nu_n=(2/kappa_2(M_n)) sum_j alpha_j^(-2) delta_{r_j}. Then nu_n is a probability measure and g_n=B_n v_n/xi^d=6 integral r^(-2)d nu_n. If fixed p>0,R<infinity give liminf_n nu_n((0,R])>=p uniformly for all beta sufficiently close to beta_c from below, the thermodynamic coupling satisfies liminf_{beta->beta_c} g_+(beta)>=6p/R^2. The uniform positive zero-mass condition for the actual 3D Ising model remains unproved. A bounded first support point alone does not supply it: nu_n=(1/n)delta_1+(1-1/n)delta_n has first point 1 but inverse-square moment tending to zero. This abstract measure example is not asserted to be an Ising zero measure.",
